  receipts: [
    "state-space conflation (an `Option`/`None` meaning >2 things — split into named variants; its most-repeated form here is **not-applicable rendered as malformed** — one reason symbol over \"the input is wrong\" and \"this strategy had nothing to say about it\", which have opposite owners and opposite repairs. ",

    "Found three times in three stages by one lane (#8801 and #8828 in body lowering, `parse_g0_tokens_remain` in parse), always by reading the producer and never from the message. ",

    "Recognition rule: if the arm sits downstream of a search, lookup or alternative that returned `Absent`, it is not-applicable and needs its own reason. ",

    "A SECOND FORM, which does not match that shape and is the same class: **a dichotomy stated over a domain with three states.** Specimen (gunbc#9324): the `floor_resource_sample` comment documented `pswpin` rising with `pgmajfault` as swap and `pgmajfault` rising with `pswpin` flat as mapping churn — two arms over three states, since BOTH FLAT is quiet. ",

    "Churn is a defect this lane owns and quiet is the absence of one, so the missing arm inverts the verdict. ",

    "The mechanism of the misread is what the recognition rule keys on: `pgmajfault rises` and `pswpin flat` are two conditions and only their CONJUNCTION is churn, so a reader matching on the cheaper condition alone selects churn for a state that satisfies `pswpin flat` and nothing else — which zero-and-zero does. ",

    "**Recognition rule for this form: for every arm of a stated dichotomy, enumerate the domain and check that each arm's conditions are required jointly.** What made it invisible rather than merely wrong is that BOTH readers landed on the same arm — 26 intervals so classified by one and 6 by another, neither having compared notes — and agreement reads as confirmation. ",

    "THAT IS A PROMPT TO RE-DERIVE, NOT A DIAGNOSTIC, and the distinction is load-bearing: convergent readings are equally produced by shared assumptions, a common heuristic, ambiguity in the subject, or one reader having anchored on the other, and n=2 on one specimen cannot separate those from a defect in the rule. ",

    "What survives is only the weaker direction — agreement between readers of one rule is not independent evidence about that rule, because the shared input is a shared potential defect, so it licenses re-deriving from the domain and never a conclusion about which cause produced it.) **A THIRD FORM, and the one that is hardest to rank because nothing is wrong today: A STATE THAT IS ALREADY LOAD-BEARING AND CARRIED AS AN AD-HOC SPELLING RATHER THAN A CONSTRUCTOR.** Specimen (2026-09-01): the identity key threaded through v1.compiler.coercion has THREE inhabitants -- a real declaring module path, the synthetic <kernel:NAME> that v1.std.core kernel_span mints for kernel nodes, and the empty string meaning unknown -- while every consumer discriminates only empty from non-empty. ",

    "lookup_checkpoint and type_realization_decision therefore read <kernel:String> as a KNOWN declaration and proceed to the spelling-keyed arm; decl_file_declares_structurally compares that synthetic identity against a roster of real paths with contains, which no <kernel:NAME> can ever match, so the structural gate is unreachable for a kernel-resolved reference BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by decision. ",

    "The key reaches those gates with exactly that value through type_reference_decl_file, from v1.compiler.emit coerce_primitive_type and v1.compiler.emit_rust rust_named_type_base and rust_applied_type_base. ",

    "**What makes this the third form rather than an instance of the first two is the evidence that the state is REAL: the tree already handles it, three times, by string prefix.** numeric_realization_declaring_modules carries the literal \"<kernel:\" as a row in a roster of MODULE PATHS; is_kernel_minted_file is a substring predicate over the same spelling; and resolved_node_is_kernel_identity_for_name owns the same fact by EXACT EQUALITY, its own note recording that a substring or prefix test is a second, weaker authority for it. THE CITED MODULE WAS WRONG AND IS NOW ALSO MOVED: no module v1.compiler.env exists; the declaration lived in v1.compiler.infer_env and was relocated (XL-0B, 2026-09-04) into v1.std.core, beside the kernel_span whose output it compares against, because v1.std.core declaration_provenance_of could not import it without closing a cycle and so re-derived the same comparison in place -- a fourth recogniser this row had not counted. Cite it at v1.std.core. The relocated body asks kernel_span; the one it replaced inlined the format literally. ",

    "**Recognition rule for this form: when a value's domain is carried in a type that cannot express one of its inhabitants, look for the inhabitant being recognised by SPELLING somewhere -- a prefix test, a magic string in a roster of real values, a sentinel. ",

    "Each such site is a consumer that already knows the state exists, and their number is the count of authorities the missing constructor has spawned.** NO WRONG ANSWER IS CLAIMED FOR THE SPECIMEN AND NONE WAS MEASURED: for the kernel names reaching those gates today the spelling-keyed answer is the correct one, which is exactly why it never surfaced -- the class is filed on the state space, not on an output, and a form that produces no incident is the one that will be found last. ",

    "**CLIMB RECEIPT (2026-09-02), appended rather than replacing the filing above, because DESIGN section 4b(4) keeps a class's discriminating evidence enrolled AFTER the climb rather than dissolving it with the production machinery.** The missing constructor now exists: std.coercion TypeDeclarationProvenance is CorpusDeclared | KernelMinted | DeclarationIdentityAbsent, minted by v1.std.core declaration_provenance_of, which decides the kernel arm by EXACT EQUALITY against kernel_span -- the minter itself -- rather than by a prefix test over its output. ",

    "All four spelling authorities this row counted are gone: the literal \"<kernel:\" row is deleted from numeric_realization_declaring_modules, is_kernel_minted_file is deleted, and the two gates that substring-compared a synthetic identity against real paths now take the coproduct, so the structural gate's unreachability for a kernel-resolved reference stops being BY CONSTRUCTION and becomes BY DECISION -- a named arm answering false. ",

    "**WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED, because this row's own honesty is the thing being climbed:** no wrong answer was found before and none is fixed now; every answer is preserved bit for bit, which is why the climb is in the STATE SPACE and not in an output. ",

    "The empty-string inhabitant is likewise gone from the channel, and the bare-table answer it used to reach silently is now the named ground GroundedByUnidentifiedBareRow, so a declared rung drop that was previously indistinguishable from a properly-keyed answer is countable and refusable. ",

    "**THE RECOGNITION RULE IS CORROBORATED AND THE CORROBORATION IS INDEPENDENT.** gunbc.type_reference_decl_file_occurrence_census reached this same four-authority set from the opposite direction -- that census asked what each of thirty-nine occurrences NEEDS, this row asked what the identity key can HOLD -- and the counts agreed. ",

    "**WHAT SURVIVES UNCLIMBED, stated so the row is not read as closed:** CorpusDeclared still carries a file path matched by contains, so the surviving arm answers WHAT A DECLARATION REALIZES AS positionally. ",

    "v1.compiler.infer_env global_bare_fallback_invariant already states the terminal key for it -- filepaths are irrelevant, the declared module path is the containment tree -- and re-keying that arm needs a declaration reference at each gate, which is a separate change.\n\n**A FOURTH FORM, MEASURED 2026-09-02 (quick-crab-396), AND IT SITS IN THE INTERPRETER RATHER THAN IN ANY MODEL: DECLARED OPTIONAL AND CONSTRUCTED ABSENT ARE TWO STATES WEARING ONE SPELLING.** A record field declared `T?` is read by authors -- and by this document's own §2 reasoning about optional carriers -- as optional-with-a-none-default. ",

    "It is not. ",

    "A literal that OMITS the field typechecks, and a later read of that field REFUSES at evaluation with `NoSuchField { type_name, field }`. ",

    "So `T?` means mandatory-at-construction-and-typed-optional, and the two states the spelling conflates are `the field is absent because the author wrote none` and `the field is absent because the literal predates it`. ",

    "EVIDENCE, a two-row probe with a positive control, which is what makes it a finding rather than a conjecture about one type: `type Widget { name: String  tag: Int? }` with `Widget { name: \"w\" }` refuses on `.tag` with `NoSuchField { type_name: \"Widget\", field: \"tag\" }`, while `Widget { name: \"w\", tag: Present { value: 3 } }.tag` reads back correctly -- so the mechanism is neither `reads fail` nor `this type is broken`, it is omission-with-no-default, and it is GENERAL to any record type. ",

    "RUNG: this is FAIL-CLOSED and explicitly NOT silent wrongness -- the interpreter refuses rather than answering the false that a reader would expect -- which is the whole of the good news and it is what sets the rung at mitigatable rather than below the ladder. ",

    "WHAT THE CORPUS CURRENTLY BELIEVES INSTEAD, and this is the reason the row exists: two carriers filed this on 2026-08-27 as `a nested compile is not evaluable in the interpreter, refusing with NoSuchField Node.ident` -- v1.tests.claim.reference_derived_disposition_census_witness_test and a sibling paragraph in v1.compiler.emit_rust. ",

    "Nested compiles are one POPULATION that happens to construct Nodes through helpers omitting v1.std.core Node's `ident` and then read it; they are not the class, and the repair that description suggests (route around the nested pipeline with a host builtin) does not touch the cause. ",

    "**POPULATION: UNENUMERATED, and stated as such rather than guessed.** It is every record type in the corpus carrying an optional field together with a literal that omits it; `v1.std.core Node.ident` is one specimen and the probe above is another. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: construction that supplies every declared field, so that a literal omitting an optional field is either unwritable or carries the absent value -- at which point the distinction between the two absences is made at construction and no read can encounter a field that was never written. ",

    "NOT REPAIRED HERE BY RULING: a defaulting change alters evaluation semantics corpus-wide and needs its own subject, population and review. ",

    "**A FIFTH FORM, MEASURED 2026-09-03, AND IT IS THE FIRST ONE WHERE THE DECLARATION ALREADY EXISTED: ONE SENTINEL CARRYING TWO FACTS WHILE A TYPED DECLARATION SAYS THEY ARE DISTINCT.** std.algebra free_monoid_collection_templates declares first and last as [ReceiverSelf] -> OptionalOf { inner: ReceiverElement }, and positional get as [ReceiverSelf, Int] -> the same. ",

    "So the result is an optional OF THE ELEMENT: where the element type is itself optional the two absences are distinct levels. ",

    "The v1 interpreter's arm bodies returned items.front().cloned().unwrap_or(Value::Null), collapsing 'the collection had no first element' and 'the first element is itself absent' into one Value::Null, because in the interpreter Null is both the absent-marker and a legal element value. ",

    "DISCRIMINATING RED, executed on both arms, not asserted: over [none, Present { value: 2 }] -- a list of length TWO whose first element is absent -- the interpreter took the OUTER Absent arm (answering 'the list is empty') while emitted Rust answered Present { Absent }. ",

    "Positive control [5,6].first() returned 5 in both. ",

    "WHAT MAKES THIS FORM DIFFERENT FROM THE PRECEDING FOUR, and why it is filed as a receipt on this row rather than as its own class: THE MISSING CONSTRUCTOR WAS NOT MISSING. ",

    "The declaration existed, was mirrored into the seed as std_algebra.rs, and was READ BY THE TYPE CHECKER -- v1.compiler.infer_method walks algebra_templates_for_profile matching on name, which is why std.target_representation representation_spelling_for typechecks with `-> RepresentationSpelling<R>?` returning `|> first` directly. ",

    "The EVALUATOR in the same binary referenced std_algebra zero times. ",

    "One binary, one declaration, the type checker honouring it and the evaluator contradicting it. ",

    "THE RUNG THIS SAT AT WAS NOT A RUNG: the interpreter did not refuse, it answered confidently and wrongly, which DESIGN section 4b places OUTSIDE the ladder. ",

    "A REPAIR EXISTS AND IS DELIBERATELY UNLANDED (gunbc#10187, DRAFT, not merged): the two arms WOULD build optional_present/optional_absent, mirroring map_lookup_as_optional, which already performs exactly this for maps -- and the reason it is withheld is the PRIOR FILING recorded below, not an unfinished implementation. ",

    "NO CLIMB IS CLAIMED BY THIS ROW. ",

    "The class stands where it stood -- 'decided by call site, not value shape, so a stored V = Optional<T> payload is never mistaken for an already-wrapped result' -- prior art in the same file rather than a new mechanism. ",

    "THE REALIZATION PICTURE IS THE PART FUTURE READERS SHOULD NOT FLATTEN, AND IT HAS THREE COLUMNS RATHER THAN ONE VERDICT. ",

    "VERIFIED BY EXECUTION: rust emission nests faithfully; and the python and typescript TYPE CONSTRUCTORS cannot carry the nesting at all -- typing.Optional[typing.Optional[int]] EVALUATES TO typing.Optional[int] and compares equal, and in the typescript realization `{0} | undefined` the absent element and the absent selection are the same value (undefined === undefined). ",

    "No method template can repair that, because the type it would have to return does not exist in those targets; a boxed encoding would be a different realization of Optional, not a better template. ",

    "REFUTED BY EXECUTION: the inference that go is faithful BECAUSE its optional row is `*{0}` and **T is a legal Go type. ",

    "The row permits the nesting and the emitter did not do it -- go emitted *int64 for a declared Optional<Optional<Int>>. ",

    "THE ROW PREDICTS CAPABILITY, NOT BEHAVIOUR, and that is the transferable lesson here: the python collapse and the go faithfulness were derived the same way, from the optional row, and only one survived execution. ",

    "UNOBSERVED: what python and go emission actually ANSWER end-to-end, because for this input neither artifact runs -- go returns two values from single-return signatures and references an undefined Present, python uses Optional and Present with neither imported nor defined. ",

    "Those sit in accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target and are UPSTREAM of this class; the denotation question is not reachable there until the artifacts compile. ",

    "NO REFUSAL IS FILED FOR THOSE PATHS AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. ",

    "A refusal on unrepresentable nesting would be a wall in front of a hole, and for typescript it would be unreachable in any case: main.rs parses only rust | python | go | dag and RenderTarget has no TypeScript variant, so no fixture can drive that path and any check over it would be permanently green by construction. ",

    "Recorded here as an OBSERVED BOUNDARY with its evidence rather than as a check that establishes nothing. ",

    "PRIOR FILING, FOUND AFTER THE REPAIR WAS WRITTEN AND BEFORE IT LANDED, WHICH IS WHY THE REPAIR IS DEFERRED RATHER THAN SHIPPED: this seam is ALREADY FILED as audit-queue item 0 of docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md (2026-08-27, from gunbc#9491), and extdeps.bmc.pid_control_decode carries the minimal reproduction inline plus an admitted workaround -- it renames its own field to magnitude on exactly this ground and claims no compiler guarantee. ",

    "Item 0 states the class as TWO questions and warns the eventual owner not to collapse them. ",

    "(1) MEMBER-SELECTION POLICY: v1.compiler.infer_lookup field_summary_for_type opens `if field == \"value\" && normed_opt` and unwraps otherwise, so FIELD ACCESS THROUGH AN OPTIONAL AUTO-UNWRAPS FOR EVERY SPELLING EXCEPT `value` -- which item 0 calls a language-semantics decision, not obviously a bug, with three candidate answers. ",

    "(2) TYPE CONFORMANCE, below floor independently of (1): a record-valued expression accepted where an Int is required. ",

    "THAT PRIOR FILING RECLASSIFIES THIS ROW'S OWN REPAIR AND THE RECLASSIFICATION IS THE POINT. ",

    "The type path ALREADY treats first() as optional and silently unwraps field access through it; the evaluator returned a bare element, so that unwrap was a no-op. ",

    "Making the evaluator construct a real Present{...} therefore does not merely expose consumers that depended on a flattening -- it makes the EVALUATOR INCONSISTENT WITH AN AUTO-UNWRAP THE TYPE CHECKER STILL PERFORMS, in the opposite direction from where the two halves started, which is not a climb. ",

    "Honouring the declaration at the evaluator requires the matching evaluator-side unwrap, and that IS item 0(1)'s open policy question. ",

    "SO THE INTERPRETER/EMITTED DIVERGENCE AND ITEM 0(1) ARE THE SAME SEAM APPROACHED FROM TWO SIDES, AND WHOEVER SETTLES THE MEMBER-SELECTION POLICY OWNS THE EVALUATOR REPAIR TOO. ",

    "Filing them as separate subjects would split one decision across two owners. ",

    "CORROBORATION FOR ITEM 0(2), independently re-derived here with a control rather than taken from the filing: four arms on a binary BUILT FROM MAIN -- `fn f() -> Bool { 5 }` refuses with 1 error (the positive control, proving the return check is not globally dead), while `fn f() -> Bool { xs().first() }` over a plain List<Int> compiles with ZERO diagnostics. ",

    "Same result under a binary containing the repair, so the gap is pre-existing and not created by any change here. ",

    "That is corroboration of a class filed five days ago and is NOT a second finding; a second row for a filed class is the nicknaming refusal at the ledger layer. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as a capability: GENERATED ARM BODIES WHOSE RETURN TYPE DERIVES FROM THE ALGEBRA TEMPLATE, so the collapse becomes unwritable rather than merely wrong. ",

    "Today the arm SELECTION is generated -- v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated.rs -- but from gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface, a roster that carries no return type and does not import std.algebra. ",

    "Two rosters name first, neither references the other, and the hand-written body honoured neither; that fork is why the arm and its declared type were separable by hand at all. ",

    "A POINTER TO ONE SPECIMEN OF THIS SHAPE IN THIS LEDGER'S OWN TOOLING, 2026-09-03: a referential-closure check over these rosters that JOINS BY NAME cannot see two declarations sharing one name whose CONTENT differs. ",

    "Measured by injection -- main's `recurrence_ledger_scoped_below_the_recurrence` duplicated with a pre-rename spelling of a symbol it cites, 9006 bytes against 8993 -- a name-grain check reports nothing rostered-undeclared and nothing declared-unrostered and PASSES, while the tree carries a citation to a symbol with zero declarations. ",

    "The guard's state space has no cell for content divergence, so its count is the same either way. ",

    "What such a check must additionally do is adjudicate any surviving duplicate against main's BYTES and REFUSE when neither copy matches, rather than resolve by position or first-wins, which is silent. ",

    "**A SIXTH FORM, whose consequence is not a bad message but a SILENT SAFETY HOLE: a `Bool` return carrying a three-valued question, where the collapsed value is the ADMITTING one.** Specimen (gunbc#10337, 2026-09-04): `where_refinement_brand_nominal_mismatch` returned `Bool` over three outcomes -- these are distinct declarations, these are the same declaration, and I CANNOT TELL which declarations these are. The third collapsed onto `false` with the second, and the consumer read `false` as admit, so a cast whose brand identity could not be determined was ACCEPTED. ",

    "The paired sentinel made it concrete: the declaration-key producer returned the empty string for a type with no declaring span and the consumer guarded on `key != \"\"`, so absence of identity was spelled as a value and read as permission. ",

    "**WHAT DISTINGUISHES THIS FORM FROM THE EARLIER ONES IS THE DIRECTION OF THE COLLAPSE.** They produce a wrong or unrankable ANSWER; this one produces NO ANSWER AT ALL on the collapsed arm, because the admitting value is indistinguishable from a genuine pass. A wall with this defect emits no diagnostic, so no red exists for review to find and no population exists to count -- the type's inadequacy is the safety hole rather than a symptom of one. ",

    "**Recognition rule for this form: for every `Bool` that gates a refusal, ask which value means UNKNOWN. If unknown shares a value with permitted, the predicate cannot refuse what it cannot determine, and the wall has a hole exactly the size of its unknown set.** ",

    "**AND A NEW DETECTION ROUTE FOR THIS CLASS, which is why the specimen is worth its length: the earlier receipts in this row were found by READING the producer. This one was invisible to reading in the strong sense -- it was read, and approved, by three separate reviews of the diff, and by its own author who had rejected the identical fail-open shape in a competing design an hour earlier.** It was settled by EXECUTING a fixture: `fn f(a: String where brand(\"x\"))` is an inline brand-carrying type with no declaration site, it parses and compiles, and it admitted one brand into a different brand -- the exact violation the wall's own refusing arm exists to catch. ",

    "Reading establishes that an arm is reachable IN PRINCIPLE; only executing establishes that the state is AUTHORABLE and that the hole is live. Per DESIGN section 4b, the authorability question is decided by what a FIXTURE can hand the compiler, never by what the accepted corpus happens to contain. ",

    "CLIMB, and it is construction rather than a better check: the key producer now returns `String?` so an undeterminable key is NOT REPRESENTABLE, and the predicate returns a four-variant `BrandNominalVerdict` so no consumer can inherit an answer from a magic value. Fixing only the sentinel would have closed the instance and left the `Bool` free to spawn the collapse again at the next consumer -- the return TYPE was the authority at fault, not the arm. ",

    "CI CHECK-RENDERING INSTANCE, 2026-09-04, import-cut lane, AND ITS RECEIPT IS THAT ONE COLLAPSED SYMBOL PRODUCED ERRORS IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. `gh pr checks` renders cancelled, failure and timed_out into a single `fail` glyph, and the dashboard digest inherits that rendering. Measured on gunbc run 33875856188: the jobs API reports required-witnesses-build, heal-generated-artifacts and required-witnesses-floor as conclusion=cancelled with a ZERO-LENGTH steps array, and the aggregating witnesses job as conclusion=failure with 3 steps -- while the rollup showed four identical fails and the digest reported the PR as failing. ",

    "THE TWO STATES HAVE OPPOSITE OWNERS AND OPPOSITE REPAIRS, which is this row's recurring form: a real red means the branch is broken and its author must fix it; a cancellation means NOTHING ABOUT THE BRANCH WAS OBSERVED and there is no signal to act on. Collapsed into one glyph, the second is indistinguishable from the first. ",

    "THE RECEIPT, and it is why this instance is worth carrying rather than being one more example: the SAME collapse has already produced the opposite error. Cancelled-read-as-PASSED merged gunbc PR 8059. Cancelled-read-as-FAILED, here, manufactures a defect in a branch nobody tested and sends an author to debug against no signal. One symbol, one rendering layer, errors in both directions -- which demonstrates that the harm is not a mis-set threshold but the conflation itself, since no reading of a symbol that means two things can be right in both cases. ",

    "REPAIR: take the verdict from the jobs API `conclusion` field, never from `gh pr checks` or a digest, and treat an EMPTY steps array or an empty log as UNOBSERVED rather than as a result. The tell that the rendering is lying is shape rather than content -- several independent jobs ending at an identical short duration, because real work does not fail identically.) ",

    "A SEVENTH FORM, AND THE ONE WORTH THE MOST BECAUSE A REPAIR PRODUCED IT (2026-09-04, import-cut lane, gunbc#10454, found by independent adjudication and confirmed in source). A review correctly refused two hand-rolled variant-to-Bool predicates over a coproduct -- the structural-equality residue DESIGN section 6 names -- and the repair replaced them with a total String projection, `unobservable_reason`, returning the refusal text or `\"\"` for the two OBSERVED verdicts. The refusal was then decided by asking whether that string was empty. So `\"\"` carried TWO meanings, this observation does not refuse and this observation refuses but recorded no reason, and an `Unobservable` with an empty reason was folded away as OBSERVED: the digest stayed empty and the command returned ExitSuccess while the roster could not testify about its subject. That is the EXACT defect the pull request existed to remove, re-entering through its own fix. ",

    "WHAT MAKES IT A DISTINCT FORM RATHER THAN ANOTHER EXAMPLE: the earlier forms are collapses that were AUTHORED. This one was INTRODUCED BY A CORRECT REPAIR of a different class, in the same motion, and it was invisible for the usual reason plus one more -- no production site constructed the bad value, so no run could exhibit it. The residue removal was right, the projection was right, and the sentinel was the only wrong part; a reviewer checking that the predicates were gone would find them gone. RECOGNITION RULE: when a repair replaces a decision with a PROJECTION, ask what the projection's empty or default value means, and whether the decision now rests on it. A refusal must be driven by the verdict, never by the presence of its prose. ",

    "AND IT SHARPENS THE AUTHORABILITY RULE THIS ROW ALREADY CARRIES. Not reachable on the corpus is not a defence: DESIGN section 4b asks whether the RED is AUTHORABLE, not whether it fires today, and a fixture constructed the empty-reason refusal in one line. THE FIRST REPAIR WAS ITSELF INSUFFICIENT AND THAT IS PART OF THE RECEIPT: driving the refusal off the canonical verdict projection only traded a reason-text sentinel for a VERDICT-LABEL sentinel, because that projection is also the renderer's word source, so a relabelled or newly added refusing state falls through a String inequality to false. The exhaustive match protected label PRODUCTION while refusal CLASSIFICATION sat on an implicit catch-all over the String domain, in the accepting path. The typed-coproduct fix is a trap -- it returns the classifier to matching variants onto true/false, the very residue whose removal started this -- so the landed shape folds to a LIST of refusing observations by a total, VALUE-RETURNING match, with nonemptiness as the condition. Exhaustiveness then sits over the DECISION rather than only the projection, and no rendered spelling decides success. The discriminating red -- a refusal with no reason must still refuse -- stays enrolled under section 4b(4) and flips alone when the text-driven form is restored, while the stale-citation red and the observed-verdict control both hold. A hole that only stays shut because nobody happens to author the bad input is not a wall, and a sentinel that moved from the prose to the label was still a sentinel.",
